# HOLDOUT SUITE — the 27 side=holdout bugs of suites/splits/semantic_split.jsonl.
# ASSEMBLED 2026-08-11; NOT YET RUN.
#
# RUN-ONCE / ANALYSE-ONLY (hard rule): this suite is run ONCE. Its output may
# be ANALYSED — differences vs the dev numbers, per-error-class tallies — but
# NOTHING may be learned from it: no code, prompt, threshold, or mechanism
# change may be derived from holdout output. Findings go to the writeup only.
#
# LEG SELECTION: for each holdout bug, one -o leg (a patch whose overfitting
# label is confirmed in suites/labels/verified_correct.jsonl) and one -c leg
# (a confirmed-correct patch), where the labels provide them. Preference:
# patch1 of the tool with the simplest provenance (plain probe divergence /
# 0-div probe; deep-dive or timing-noise provenance only when it is the only
# verified patch for that side). Everything in verified_incorrect.jsonl and
# excluded.jsonl is dropped. All 35 patchfile paths verified present on the
# VM (ssh hetzner, read-only) 2026-08-11.
#
# SKIPPED SIDES (no verified label for that side; one line each):
#   Chart-8-o     no Doverfitting patch verified (overfit_legs=0 in split)
#   Closure-31-o  no Doverfitting patch verified (overfit_legs=0)
#   Closure-57-o  no Doverfitting patch verified (overfit_legs=0)
#   Closure-115-o only Doverfitting patch (ssFix-plausible) is
