#   hard legs, kept deliberately.
# - Lang-55-c (Jaid patch1-Lang-55-Jaid.patch): StopWatch bug — probe
#   value-div on this bug's other correct patches was certified TIMING
#   NOISE; a value-relation FP here would land in that known class.
#
# THE PRE-REGISTERED READ (registered BEFORE launch; numbers pasted
# verbatim afterwards, per the verbatim-numbers rule):
# (1) AGGREGATE P/R vs the dev baseline P=0.77 / R=0.62 (diag-24, gpt-5.4).
#     Read is the DIFFERENCE, with the caveat that this holdout skews
#     correct-heavy (23c/12o) vs dev, so R rests on only 12 overfit legs.
# (2) PER-FP-CLASS TALLY on the 23 -c legs, into the three known classes:
#     (a) Math-65-type formula/indiscriminate relation FPs,
#     (b) Chart-type valid-by-construction FPs,
#     (c) generic-exception leaks (Lang-27-type).
#     Plus a residual "new class" bucket — new classes are a writeup
#     finding, NOT a fix ticket.
# (3) PER-FN-FAMILY TALLY on the 12 -o legs, against the witness-study gap
#     families (8.33): classify each miss by whether the ground-truth
#     witness is patched-side-input-reach shaped (draw-05/8.32 family),
#     cross-thread/state-carrying, or other; tally, no mechanism change.
# (4) Fail-closed checks recorded as always (gate VOIDs on overfit legs);
#     on the holdout even a hard stop is a WRITEUP FINDING, not a
#     stop-and-fix.
#
# LEGS: 35 (12 -o + 23 -c). Expected cost at ~130k tokens/leg: ~4.55M tokens.
# Flags: n=5/m=12, NO --divcap — identical COMMON to stack_confirm.cases.
